B - Flip Card Stack  / 
Time Limit: 2 sec / Memory Limit: 1024 MiB
Score : 
200 points
Problem Statement
There are 
N cards numbered 
1 to 
N, each with a distinguishable front and back. Initially, they are stacked in the order 
1,2,…,N from the top, all face up.
Takahashi performs 
Q operations on this stack. The 
i-th operation 
(1≤i≤Q) is as follows.
Flip the top 
Ki cards over together as a single block and put them back in place.
This reverses the top-to-bottom order of the top Ki
​cards and also turns each of those cards over.
Find the order and orientation of the cards after all operations.Specifically, for each i=1,2,…,N, let 
Xi be the number written on the 
i-th card from the top; print Xi if that card is face up, and −Xi
​if it is face down.
Constraints
1≤N,Q≤100
1≤Ki≤N All input values are integers.
Input
The input is given from Standard Input in the following format:
N 
Q
K1,K2...KQ
​Output
Print 
N lines. For the 
i-th line 
(1≤i≤N), let Xi be the number written on the i-th card from the top after the Q operations; print Xi
​if that card is face up, and −Xi if it is face down.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
solution code:
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int n, q;
    cin >> n >> q;

    int a[105];
    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        a[i] = i + 1;
    }

    for(int x = 0; x < q; x++) {
        int k;
        cin >> k;
        int i = 0;
        int j = k - 1;

        while(i < j) {
            int temp = a[i];
            a[i] = a[j];
            a[j] = temp;

            i++;
            j--;
        }
        for(int i = 0; i < k; i++) {
            a[i] = -a[i];
        }
    }
    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        cout << a[i] << endl;
    }

    return 0;
}

